cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use K-FRAG in your research, please cite this software and the associated paper when available."

title: "K-FRAG V4.15: Fragment-Based Authenticated Image Watermarking with Blind Crop Recovery"

type: software

version: "4.15"

date-released: "2026-11-02"

authors:
  - family-names: "NICHOLAS"
    given-names: "NATALIA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Natalia2-pixel/K-FRAG"

url: "https://github.com/Natalia2-pixel/K-FRAG"

license: "Apache-2.0"

keywords:
  - watermarking
  - image watermarking
  - robust watermarking
  - authenticated watermarking
  - provenance
  - image authentication
  - crop robustness
  - blind synchronization
  - Reed-Solomon
  - HMAC
  - computer vision
  - deep learning

abstract: >
  K-FRAG V4.15 is a fragment-based authenticated image-watermarking
  system designed for robust provenance recovery from full images and
  cropped image fragments. The released runtime includes authenticated
  watermark issuance and embedding, independent fragment decoding,
  structure-aware fusion, regional refinement, Reed-Solomon recovery,
  cryptographic authentication, blind spatial synchronization, and
  authenticated crop recovery.
